# Read the page, then hold the sandbox open while the host looks at it.
#
# The taint bit is only observable from outside while the sandbox exists, so this file
# exists to keep one alive across the control call. The marker file is how the two
# sides agree on the ordering without a sleep race -- the same trick rung 1 uses for
# mid-task attenuation, and it grants the agent nothing: the marker arrives in a
# directory it can already read and tells it nothing it could act on.

read-source /untrusted/injected-page.txt --obey-instructions

wait-for /scratch/observed --timeout 60

# After the host has read the bit. Still refused -- observing a sandbox does not
# change it, and there is no control call that would.
call-broker --tag after-observe read_wiki deploy-runbook
